WEBVTT

00:00:00.408 --> 00:00:09.112
In this video, you will add a lighting company as the presenting installer of your contest, and see how neighbors can ask them for a quote with one tap.

00:00:09.112 --> 00:00:10.115
We start on the map.

00:00:11.069 --> 00:00:12.743
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:15.618 --> 00:00:18.168
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:19.863 --> 00:00:20.843
Then tap Allow.

00:00:24.519 --> 00:00:27.729
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:27.729 --> 00:00:30.509
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:35.072
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:35.072 --> 00:00:35.773
Tap it.

00:00:37.311 --> 00:00:39.274
In the menu, tap Your contests.

00:00:41.905 --> 00:00:46.001
That is where the contests you run, and the homes you entered, live.

00:00:46.001 --> 00:00:46.858
Tap Mine.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.630
This is your personal page.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:56.102
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:00:56.102 --> 00:00:58.211
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:04.043
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:04.043 --> 00:01:10.664
A lighting company can sponsor your contest as its presenting installer, and neighbors can ask them for a quote.

00:01:10.664 --> 00:01:16.638
This is set up on the Details tab, so tap Details, and scroll down to Presenting installer.

00:01:18.321 --> 00:01:20.012
Type the company's name.

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:23.538
Then the email address where quote requests should go.

00:01:23.538 --> 00:01:29.564
That is the address the company checks for new customers, and each request is emailed to you as well.

00:01:29.564 --> 00:01:30.897
And add their website.

00:01:33.695 --> 00:01:35.059
Tap Save changes.

00:01:37.091 --> 00:01:45.345
This adds a Get a quote button to your contest page, so families who love the lights can ask the company for the same thing at their own home.

00:01:45.345 --> 00:01:48.439
The button shows only while your contest is live.

00:01:49.294 --> 00:01:51.334
Now let's see it from a neighbor's side.

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:53.055
They open the contest page.

00:01:53.055 --> 00:01:55.013
They need to be signed in to ask.

00:01:55.013 --> 00:01:56.344
Then they tap Get a quote.

00:01:58.032 --> 00:02:02.772
They add their name, a phone number if they like, and describe what they would like done.

00:02:02.772 --> 00:02:06.763
They must tick the box that says they agree to share their details.

00:02:06.763 --> 00:02:09.141
Without that tick, nothing is sent.

00:02:09.141 --> 00:02:10.891
Then they tap Send request.

00:02:12.646 --> 00:02:18.618
The request goes to the company and to you, the contest organizer, and SoCal Lights keeps a copy.

00:02:19.531 --> 00:02:22.358
Back on your side, open the Promote tab.

00:02:22.358 --> 00:02:26.427
Every quote request is listed there, with the neighbor's name and details.

00:02:28.163 --> 00:02:31.079
Next up: Installer profiles and Installed by.
